  (:adr/body
  "# ADR-2607184700: Transport negative matrix and high-level web runtime parity

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-18

## Decision

Qualify affine and framing failures as executable behavior: a second close of
the same handle returns minus one; TLS server-name mismatch consumes and closes
the TCP handle; slow reads terminate under the finite socket timeout; and a
17x17 Content-Length/body-size matrix accepts every complete body and rejects
every partial one under the actual compiled Kotoba parser.

Browser and Node parity is defined at the safe high-level component boundary,
not by exposing raw sockets. The JavaScript host contract now recognizes the
full declared import catalog and links `http_get` only when an explicit
synchronous bridge is injected. It supplies exact host, port, path, maximum
response bytes and manual redirect policy. Absence of that bridge leaves the
import unavailable.

## Maturity boundary

This closes the first negative matrix and high-level HTTP parity seam. It does
not prove DNS rebinding resistance after resolution, external PKI/revocation,
case-insensitive/duplicate HTTP framing headers, chunked decoding, concurrent
linker stress, or a real browser SharedArrayBuffer deployment.
")))
